EXPERIMENT 05: MAVEN CI/CD PIPELINE

STEP 1: Create a folder named maven on the Desktop and open it in VS Code.

STEP 2: Open the terminal and generate the Maven project using:

mvnw.cmd org.apache.maven.plugins:maven-archetype-plugin:3.1.2:generate -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -DarchetypeGroupId=org.apache.maven.archetypes -DarchetypeVersion=1.4 -DgroupId=com.example -DartifactId=demo -DoutputDirectory=C:\Users\deepnitha\Desktop\maven

Press Enter to accept the default version.

STEP 3: Inside the maven folder, create the folders .github/workflows. Create a file named maven.yml inside .github/workflows and paste:

name: Java CI/CD Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches: ["main"]
  pull_request:
    branches: ["main"]
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Set up JDK 21
        uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          java-version: '21'
          distribution: 'temurin'

      - name: Compile Java Program
        run: javac new.java

Save the file.

STEP 4: Create new.java in the maven folder and save the Java program.

STEP 5: Open the terminal in the maven folder and execute these commands one by one:

git init
git config --global user.name "kavya080206-stack"
git config --global user.email "YOUR_GITHUB_EMAIL"
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Initial"
git branch -M main

STEP 6: Create a GitHub repository named mavenjava. Connect it by executing:

git remote add origin https://github.com/kavya080206-stack/mavenjava.git
git remote -v

STEP 7: Push the project to GitHub:

git push -u origin main

STEP 8: Verify the workflow:
1. Open the mavenjava repository on GitHub.
2. Click Actions.
3. Open the workflow run.
4. Check for the green tick mark.

RESULT: The project was pushed to GitHub, and the GitHub Actions workflow executed successfully.
